To create a user ID, you should choose a non-human-identifiable ID that does not change throughout the customer lifecycle. For example, avoid using personal information like email addresses. The user ID can be set in the JSON Web Token if security is enabled. 

For web chat, you can set the value of the user_id property in your integration code. Here’s a basic example of how to set a user ID in the web chat integration:

```javascript
<script>
window.watsonAssistantChatOptions = {
    integrationID: 'YOUR_INTEGRATION_ID',
    region: 'YOUR_REGION',
    serviceInstanceID: 'YOUR_SERVICE_INSTANCE',
    cloudPrivateHostURL: 'YOUR_HOST_URL',
    onLoad: function(instance) {
        instance.updateUserID('YOUR_UNIQUE_USER_ID'); // Replace with your unique user ID
        instance.render();
    }
};
</script>
```

In this example, replace `'YOUR_UNIQUE_USER_ID'` with the ID you want to use. If you do not pass an identifier for the user when the session begins, the web chat will create a randomized universally unique ID for you.

